UID:camargo-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T015916Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Camargo Fellowship 2027-2028 for Artists\, Scholars and T
 hinkers (Cassis\, France)
DESCRIPTION:The Camargo Foundation invites artists\, scholars and thinkers 
 to its flagship Core Fellowship: a ten-week self-directed residency on its
  clifftop campus overlooking the Mediterranean in Cassis\, France\, dedica
 ted to research\, experimentation and interdisciplinary exchange. Curators
  apply under the Thinkers category\, which covers accomplished professiona
 ls and practitioners in cultural and creative fields who are professionall
 y engaged in critical thought\, including curators\, critics and journalis
 ts\; projects should engage theoretical\, artistic or societal questions. 
 WHAT YOU GET: a stipend of EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 total)\, basic tra
 nsportation funding\, and a furnished apartment with an equipped kitchen o
 n campus. Fourteen fellowships are awarded per year: seven for artists and
  seven for scholars and thinkers. RESIDENCY PERIODS: Fall 2027 (8 Septembe
 r to 17 November 2027) or Spring 2028 (23 February to 4 May 2028). ELIGIBI
 LITY: artists in visual arts\, performance\, writing\, film\, music or mul
 tidisciplinary work with at least 5 years of professional practice\; schol
 ars holding or pursuing a PhD focused on French and Francophone cultures o
 r cross-cultural Mediterranean studies\; and thinkers as described above. 
 APPLICATION: via Submittable with a 100-word proposal summary\, a 1\,200-w
 ord proposal narrative\, a 300-word rationale for Camargo\, a 300-word car
 eer-stage rationale\, a CV (max 3 pages)\, work samples and two references
 . NOTE: the foundation has announced that this is the final Fellowship sel
 ected through a public open call until further notice\; a new selection pr
 ocess begins in July 2027\, making this the last chance to apply directly.
 \n\nOrganisation: Camargo Foundation\nLocation: Camargo Foundation campus\
 , Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.\nAward: EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 to
 tal for the ten-week residency)\, plus basic travel funding and a furnishe
 d apartment with equipped kitchen on the Camargo campus. 14 fellowships pe
 r year: 7 for artists and 7 for scholars and thinkers. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Ten weeks\, either 8 September to 17 November 2027 or 23 Febru
 ary to 4 May 2028.\n\nMore: https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fello
 wship-2026-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Camargo Foundation campus\, Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bow-seat-true-blue-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261007T015916Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: True Blue Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:Bow Seat's True Blue Fellowship funds youth-led projects that u
 se the creative arts as their primary method for building awareness or dri
 ving action on ocean\, waterways and climate change issues\, including env
 ironmental justice. Twelve fellows are selected each year and receive up t
 o USD 2\,500 in project funding alongside mentorship\, capacity-building p
 rogramming\, and access to a peer community that includes the Future Blue 
 Youth Council and Bow Seat staff. ELIGIBILITY: youth worldwide aged 16 to 
 24 at the start of the fellowship period in January. Individuals\, groups 
 and youth-led organisations may apply\, with one designated project leader
  for a group. Projects must be new or emerging\, meaning less than two yea
 rs old\, and should span at least one year running January to December. Ap
 plications must be submitted in English\, though translation tools are acc
 eptable\, and applicants should be comfortable with spoken English for pee
 r collaboration. NOTE: this is a youth programme with an upper age limit o
 f 24\, and the creative-arts requirement is central rather than incidental
 \, so proposals built on other methods are out of scope. Deadline 30 Augus
 t 2026 at 11:59pm ET.\n\nOrganisation: Bow Seat Ocean Awareness Programs\n
 Location: Remote\, open to youth worldwide.\nAward: Up to USD 2\,500 in pr
 oject funding per fellow\, plus mentorship and capacity-building programmi
 ng. Twelve youth are selected annually. No application fee.\nDuration: One
  year\, January to December 2027\n\nMore: https://bowseat.org/programs/tru
 e-blue-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://bowseat.org/programs/true-blue-fellowship/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, open to youth worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
